WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 8: Wonderful Water.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.280
In this unit, your child learns about water
— where it comes from, where we find it,

3
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.400
and all the ways we use it every day.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.260
They meet rainy and sunny weather, animals that live in water,

5
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.920
and the big idea that water is a gift we should not waste.

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.760
The goal is warm, confident English and a
thankful heart for water — not perfect spelling.

7
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.660
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.840
By the end of this unit, you will be able to say
why plants, animals, and people all need water.

9
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.020
you will also name places where we
find water (rain, river, sea, well).

10
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:50.500
you will also say how we use water:
“i use water to drink / wash / cook.”.

11
00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.260
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.920
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: water, rain, drop, wet, dry, clean.

13
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.400
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.280
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.580
The reading sequence includes The Well in
the Village and Talk about Wonderful Water.

16
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:15.980
Read actively.

17
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.260
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.120
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.660
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

20
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.780
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: I use water to ___.

21
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:42.700
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

22
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.920
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

23
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:51.000
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

24
00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.580
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

25
00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.880
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

26
00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.360
You are ready to begin.

27
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:05.740
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

28
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.420
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

29
00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.000
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
